# Quality, security & Git

## Quality

- TypeScript `strict` (avoid `any`). Structured errors to the UI — no stack traces in the browser.
- Before PR: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm format:check`, `pnpm build`. Format with `pnpm format`.
- If DB/infra touched: ensure `pnpm docker:up` (or `pnpm db:migrate` with `db` already running) succeeds.

## Security

- Secrets in `.env` only — never `NEXT_PUBLIC_` for provider keys or DB passwords.
- Do not commit `.env`, `.env.local`, secrets, caches, or local runtime files. `.env.example` is allowed.
- `.cursor/rules` are committed so the team shares conventions.

## Git

- Branch flow: `feature/* → PR → develop → PR → main`.
- `main` is stable; `develop` is the active integration branch.
- Branch `feature/<short-kebab-name>` from `develop`. No direct commits/pushes to `main` or `develop` — both are protected by GitHub Rulesets (PR required).
- Prefer release PRs into `main` from `develop` only.
- Commit only when explicitly requested. Conventional Commits (`feat` / `fix` / `refactor` / `docs` / `chore`): imperative summary + optional 1–2 sentence body.
- PR body follows `.github/pull_request_template.md`; run checks for touched areas first.
